hw/sh4: ze0 2DG op 0x82 after a 0xd0 polygon: repeat the pattern, mask by the polygon (M8.C1u).

Map areas (water, parks, forest) are drawn as 0xe0 (polygon box),
0xd0 (N vertices), 0x82 (a 32x32 pattern texture over the box), then
0xb3 (outline from the same vertex array). The London start screen has
160 of these 0x82 after a 0xd0, against 9 plain 0x80 covers (op dump,
EXP-2026-11-23-M8.C1u-2dg-area-pattern). texquad() stretched the
32x32 pattern over the whole box and ignored the polygon, so every
area showed as a coarse, pixelated rectangle while its outline had the
right shape. Now a 0x82 that follows a 0xd0 repeats the texture from
the quad's corner and writes only pixels inside the polygon (even-odd,
as fill_poly). Without a pending polygon (UI images) it stretches as
before.

This file sorts after ze0-h46 on purpose: it is made against the tree
with every earlier patch applied (h32 and h46 also touch ze0_2dg.c).

Signed-off-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>

